/Title (From a neurodevelopmental perspective, these processes represent adaptive regulatory attempts rather than diagn-     -ostic indicators in isolation \(Schore, 2003; Siegel, 2012\). Severe psychiatric conditions such as bipolar spectrum disorders, psychotic disorders, or neurological dysregulation require clinical diagnosis & may necessitate pharmacological stabilisation. However, research in trauma psychology suggests that many individuals presenting for mental health care exhibit unresolved trauma responses, attachment disruption, or chronic stress activation rather than primary psychiatric disease \(Herman, 1992; van der Kolk, 2014\).)
